Content:
Summary of findings:
- Computed spatial-heterogeneity t-statistics for 351 genes across 22 annotated cell types from `dataset_lohoff_et_al_seqfish.h5ad`.
- The long-format table contains 7,722 rows: one t-statistic per gene-cell type pair.
- Cell types were ordered by mean t-statistic. The top five by average t-statistic were:
  1. Forebrain/Midbrain/Hindbrain — 15.481
  2. Spinal cord — 13.744
  3. Gut tube — 9.645
  4. Lateral plate mesoderm — 8.678
  5. Low quality — 7.866

Decisions & assumptions:
- Used `obs['celltype_mapped_refined']` as the cell-type annotation.
- Parsed embryo and z-slice covariates from observation names such as `embryo1_Pos0_cell10_z2`.
- Only one embryo, `embryo1`, is present, so embryo and embryo:z interaction terms are not separately estimable; the fitted adjustment effectively includes intercept plus z-slice.
- The h5ad object had no precomputed neighborhood graph in `obsp`, so I reconstructed a spatial cell-cell neighborhood network per cell type using Delaunay triangulation on `obsm['spatial']`.
- The spatial covariate was computed as the row-normalized inverse-shortest-path weighted average of same-gene expression across other cells of the same cell type.
- Added a plotting-facing alias `Mesenchyme` for `Mixed mesenchymal mesoderm` while retaining the original cell-type label.

Artifacts:
- `project/outputs/tables/lohoff_2e_t_statistics_long.csv`
- `project/outputs/tables/lohoff_2e_average_t_statistics.csv`
- `project/outputs/reports/lohoff_2e_statistical_method_summary.md`
- `project/outputs/scripts/compute_lohoff_2e_stats.py`

