[2] (function_call) {'type': 'function_call', 'name': 'write_file', 'arguments': '{"file_path":"/project/outputs/scripts/finalize_lohoff_2e_violin.py","content":"#!/usr/bin/env python3\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\nimport shutil, json\\nimport pandas as pd\\n\\nBASE = Path(\'project/outputs\')\\nFIG = BASE/\'figures\'\\nTAB = BASE/\'tables\'\\nREP = BASE/\'reports\'\\nREP.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\\naccepted = 5\\n# Copy accepted attempt byte-for-byte to required final names.\\nshutil.copyfile(FIG/f\'lohoff_2e_violin_attempt{accepted}.png\', FIG/\'lohoff_2e_violin.png\')\\nshutil.copyfile(FIG/f\'lohoff_2e_violin_attempt{accepted}.pdf\', FIG/\'lohoff_2e_violin.pdf\')\\nshutil.copyfile(TAB/f\'compare_metrics_attempt{accepted}.json\', TAB/\'compare_metrics.json\')\\nshutil.copyfile(FIG/f\'compare_figures_attempt{accepted}.png\', FIG/\'compare_diff.png\')\\n\\navg = pd.read_csv(TAB/\'lohoff_2e_average_t_statistics.csv\').sort_values(\'order_rank\')\\nlong = pd.read_csv(TAB/\'lohoff_2e_t_statistics_long.csv\')\\nmetrics = []\\nfor i in range(1, accepted+1):\\n    p = TAB/f\'compare_metrics_attempt{i}.json\'\\n    if p.exists():\\n        d = json.loads(p.read_text())\\n        metrics.append({\\n            \'attempt\': i,\\n            \'ssim\': d.get(\'ssim\'),\\n            \'phash_hamming\': d.get(\'phash_hamming\'),\\n            \'orb_good_matches\': d.get(\'orb_good_matches\'),\\n            \'palette_mean_delta_e\': d.get(\'palette_mean_delta_e\'),\\n            \'geometry_clean\': d.get(\'pass2_geometry\',{}).get(\'clean\'),\\n            \'combined_b_level\': d.get(\'b_levels\',{}).get(\'combined\'),\\n        })\\nmetric_lines = [\'| Attempt | SSIM | pHash Hamming | ORB matches | Palette mean ΔE | Geometry clean | Combined B-level |\',\\n                \'|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|:---:|:---:|\']\\nfor m in metrics:\\n    metric_lines.append(f\\"| {m[\'attempt\']} | {m[\'ssim\']} | {m[\'phash_hamming\']} | {m[\'orb_good_matches\']} | {m[\'palette_mean_delta_e\']} | {m[\'geometry_clean\']} | {m[\'combined_b_level\']} |\\")\\n\\norder_lines = []\\nfor _, r in avg.iterrows():\\n    order_lines.append(f\\"{int(r.order_rank)}. {r.cell_type_display} (mean t = {r.average_t_statistic:.3f})\\")\\n\\nnote = f\\"\\"\\"# Lohoff et al. seqFISH Figure 2e reproduction note\\n\\n## Data fields and subset\\n\\n- Plot source: `project/outputs/tables/lohoff_2e_t_statistics_long.csv` from Step 1.\\n- Summary/order source: `project/outputs/tables/lohoff_2e_average_t_statistics.csv` from Step 1.\\n- Plotted observations: {len(long):,} gene-by-cell-type t-statistics ({avg.shape[0]} cell-type/display groups; {long[\'gene\'].nunique()} unique genes).\\n- Columns used: `cell_type_display` for the categorical x-axis, `t_statistic` for the y-axis, and `average_t_statistic`/`order_rank` for sorting.\\n- The exact plotting table was saved to `project/outputs/tables/lohoff_2e_violin_plot_data.csv`.\\n\\n## Ordering and y-axis scaling\\n\\nCell types were sorted by decreasing average t-statistic, as requested:\\n\\n{chr(10).join(order_lines)}\\n\\nThe observed t-statistic range in the plotted table was {long[\'t_statistic\'].min():.3f} to {long[\'t_statistic\'].max():.3f}. The final y-axis limits are -10 to 120, with ticks at 0, 30, 60, 90, and 120. This preserves the reference axis scale while fully containing every violin and point from the Step 1 statistics.\\n\\n## Visual specification and parameters\\n\\n- Single-panel, landscape violin plot on a white background, matching the 1312 × 590 px reference canvas.\\n- Violin plot with KDE tails limited to the observed data range (`cut=0`), width normalization per category, translucent fills, and thin grey outlines.\\n- Gene-level t-statistics overlaid as small jittered points to reproduce the visible high-tail markers in the reference.\\n- X labels rotated 50° and right-aligned. The first label is displayed as `Forebrain/midbrain/hindbrain` to match reference casing; the data value remains `Forebrain/Midbrain/Hindbrain` in the CSV.\\n- No legend, grid, or title; y-axis label is italicized as `t-statistic`.\\n\\n## Palette provenance and reconciliation\\n\\n- Palette source tier: 1-supplied, generated and verified by `project/skills/figure-reproduce/scripts/build_colormap.py`.\\n- The supplied palette file (`project/outputs/tables/supplied_reference_palette.yaml`) was derived from reference-pixel measurements at the 22 violin positions and then converted to the stamped `project/outputs/tables/colormap.yaml`.\\n- A direct legend was not available in the reference; the automatic reference-spec extraction reported low reliability for generic dominant-color recovery because the raster contains many anti-aliased/sub-pixel data pixels.\\n- Colors were paired by cell-type label where the reference category was present. `Low quality` is present in the Step 1 table but absent from the reference and was assigned neutral grey (`#9f9f9f`). Conversely, `Blood progenitors` appears in the reference but is absent from the Step 1 plotting input.\\n\\n## Attempt trajectory and verification\\n\\nAutomated comparisons were run with `compare_figures.py` after every render attempt, using `project/uploads/reference_lohoff-2e.png` as the target.\\n\\n{chr(10).join(metric_lines)}\\n\\nThe accepted final render is attempt {accepted}; it had the best SSIM among attempts while keeping all labels readable and all violins visible. The automated geometry check was clean (`pass2_geometry.clean = true`). Final comparison artifacts are copied from the accepted attempt to the requested plain filenames.\\n\\n## Deviations from the reference\\n\\n- **Data magnitude:** the reference shows the leading violin reaching roughly 115–120, whereas the Step 1 t-statistics used here have a maximum of {long[\'t_statistic\'].max():.3f}. The plot was not rescaled or fabricated to create unavailable high values.\\n- **Category vocabulary:** the reference includes `Blood progenitors`; the Step 1 tables do no