 1  # Lohoff et al. seqFISH Figure 2e reproduction note
 2  
 3  ## Data fields and subset
 4  
 5  - Plot source: `project/outputs/tables/lohoff_2e_t_statistics_long.csv` from Step 1.
 6  - Summary/order source: `project/outputs/tables/lohoff_2e_average_t_statistics.csv` from Step 1.
 7  - Plotted observations: 7,722 gene-by-cell-type t-statistics (22 cell-type/display groups; 351 unique genes).
 8  - Columns used: `cell_type_display` for the categorical x-axis, `t_statistic` for the y-axis, and `average_t_statistic`/`order_rank` for sorting.
 9  - The exact plotting table was saved to `project/outputs/tables/lohoff_2e_violin_plot_data.csv`.
10  
11  ## Ordering and y-axis scaling
12  
13  Cell types were sorted by decreasing average t-statistic, as requested:
14  
15  1. Forebrain/Midbrain/Hindbrain (mean t = 15.481)
16  2. Spinal cord (mean t = 13.744)
17  3. Gut tube (mean t = 9.645)
18  4. Lateral plate mesoderm (mean t = 8.678)
19  5. Low quality (mean t = 7.866)
20  6. Splanchnic mesoderm (mean t = 7.835)
21  7. Surface ectoderm (mean t = 6.558)
22  8. Intermediate mesoderm (mean t = 6.457)
23  9. Endothelium (mean t = 6.372)
24  10. Neural crest (mean t = 6.371)
25  11. Haematoendothelial progenitors (mean t = 5.453)
26  12. Mesenchyme (mean t = 5.339)
27  13. Cardiomyocytes (mean t = 5.141)
28  14. Dermomyotome (mean t = 4.581)
29  15. Cranial mesoderm (mean t = 3.631)
30  16. Presomitic mesoderm (mean t = 2.739)
31  17. Erythroid (mean t = 1.225)
32  18. Definitive endoderm (mean t = 0.832)
33  19. Anterior somitic tissues (mean t = 0.449)
34  20. Allantois (mean t = 0.065)
35  21. NMP (mean t = -0.103)
36  22. Sclerotome (mean t = -0.591)
37  
38  The observed t-statistic range in the plotted table was -8.633 to 54.286. The final y-axis limits are -10 to 120, with ticks at 0, 30, 60, 90, and 120. This preserves the reference axis scale while fully containing every violin and point from the Step 1 statistics.
39  
40  ## Visual specification and parameters
41  
42  - Single-panel, landscape violin plot on a white background, matching the 1312 × 590 px reference canvas.
43  - Violin plot with KDE tails limited to the observed data range (`cut=0`), width normalization per category, translucent fills, and thin grey outlines.
44  - Gene-level t-statistics overlaid as small jittered points to reproduce the visible high-tail markers in the reference.
45  - X labels rotated 50° and right-aligned. The first label is displayed as `Forebrain/midbrain/hindbrain` to match reference casing; the data value remains `Forebrain/Midbrain/Hindbrain` in the CSV.
46  - No legend, grid, or title; y-axis label is italicized as `t-statistic`.
47  
48  ## Palette provenance and reconciliation
49  
50  - Palette source tier: 1-supplied, generated and verified by `project/skills/figure-reproduce/scripts/build_colormap.py`.
51  - The supplied palette file (`project/outputs/tables/supplied_reference_palette.yaml`) was derived from reference-pixel measurements at the 22 violin positions and then converted to the stamped `project/outputs/tables/colormap.yaml`.
52  - A direct legend was not available in the reference; the automatic reference-spec extraction reported low reliability for generic dominant-color recovery because the raster contains many anti-aliased/sub-pixel data pixels.
53  - Colors were paired by cell-type label where the reference category was present. `Low quality` is present in the Step 1 table but absent from the reference and was assigned neutral grey (`#9f9f9f`). Conversely, `Blood progenitors` appears in the reference but is absent from the Step 1 plotting input.
54  
55  ## Attempt trajectory and verification
