Content:
ToolCalls:
  1. {'name': 'write', 'args': {'file_path': 'reports/lohoff_2e_report.md', 'contents': "# Lohoff et al. seqFISH spatial heterogeneity violin plot\n\n## Title & Objective\nCreate a Lohoff Fig. 2e-style violin plot showing, for each cell type, the distribution across genes of the linear-model *t*-statistic for the spatial weighted-expression covariate. Cell types were sorted by decreasing average *t*-statistic, and the y-axis was scaled so all violins and overlaid gene-level points are fully visible.\n\n## Data & Methods\n- **Input dataset:** `library/datasets/dataset_lohoff_et_al_seqfish.h5ad`\n- **Expression matrix:** 19,416 cells × 351 genes from `adata.X`.\n- **Cell-type labels:** `obs['celltype_mapped_refined']`, yielding 22 plotted groups.\n- **Spatial coordinates:** `obsm['spatial']`.\n- **Covariates:** embryo and z-slice parsed from observation names; only `embryo1` was present, so the estimable non-spatial adjustment was effectively intercept plus z-slice where both slices were present.\n- **Spatial covariate:** for each cell type and gene, a same-gene weighted mean over other cells of the same cell type was computed using inverse shortest-path distance on a reconstructed Delaunay cell-cell neighborhood graph; rows were normalized to form weighted means.\n- **Model:** for each gene within each cell type, expression was regressed on spatial weighted expression plus available embryo/z covariates. The reported statistic is the *t*-statistic for the spatial weighted-expression coefficient.\n- **Plotting:** 7,722 gene-by-cell-type *t*-statistics were plotted as violins with overlaid jittered gene-level points. Cell types were sorted by average *t*-statistic. Final y-axis limits were `-10` to `120` with ticks at `0, 30, 60, 90, 120`.\n\n## Results\n- Computed **7,722** gene-cell type statistics: **351 genes × 22 cell types**.\n- The observed plotted *t*-statistic range was **-8.633 to 54.286**; the selected y-axis fully contains all data while retaining the reference figure scale.\n- Highest mean spatial heterogeneity *t*-statistics:\n  1. Forebrain/Midbrain/Hindbrain — mean *t* = **15.481**\n  2. Spinal cord — mean *t* = **13.744**\n  3. Gut tube — mean *t* = **9.645**\n  4. Lateral plate mesoderm — mean *t* = **8.678**\n  5. Low quality — mean *t* = **7.866**\n- Lowest mean *t*-statistics were NMP (**-0.103**) and Sclerotome (**-0.591**).\n- The final accepted figure was render attempt 5, with automated comparison against the reference reporting **SSIM = 0.7245**, pHash Hamming distance **16**, and **167** ORB good matches.\n\n### Key figure\n![Lohoff 2e violin plot](../figures/lohoff_2e_violin.png)\n\n## Caveats & Warnings\n- The staged dataset contains only one embryo (`embryo1`), so embryo main effects and embryo:z interactions from the written methodology were not separately estimable; results are adjusted only for the available estimable covariates.\n- The h5ad file did not contain a precomputed neighborhood graph in `obsp`; a Delaunay graph from `obsm['spatial']` was reconstructed, which may not exactly match the graph used in the reference analysis.\n- The computed *t*-statistics max out at ~54.3, whereas the reference image shows a leading violin extending near 115–120; the final plot preserves the computed values and does not rescale/fabricate the data.\n- The dataset-derived categories include `Low quality` but not `Blood progenitors`, so one displayed category necessarily differs from the supplied reference image.\n- The final category order follows the user-requested average *t*-statistic sorting, which differs in places from the reference figure order.\n\n## Next Steps\n- If a precomputed Lohoff cell-cell neighborhood graph or multi-embryo dataset is available, rerun the statistic computation to more closely reproduce the original analysis.\n- Optionally repeat the plot with a tighter y-axis such as ~`-10` to `60` for improved visual separation of the computed distributions, while retaining the current version as the reference-scale rendering.\n- Inspect genes in the high-tail points for top-ranked cell types to identify specific markers driving spatial residual heterogeneity.\n\n## Artifacts\n- Final PNG figure: `project/outputs/figures/lohoff_2e_violin.png`\n- Final PDF figure: `project/outputs/figures/lohoff_2e_violin.pdf`\n- Long-format t-statistics: `project/outputs/tables/lohoff_2e_t_statistics_long.csv`\n- Average/order summary: `project/outputs/tables/lohoff_2e_average_t_statistics.csv`\n- Exact plotting data: `project/outputs/tables/lohoff_2e_violin_plot_data.csv`\n- Figure color map: `project/outputs/tables/colormap.yaml`\n- Reference comparison metrics: `project/outputs/tables/compare_metrics.json`\n- Visual diff/comparison: `project/outputs/figures/compare_diff.png`\n- Statistical method summary: `project/outputs/reports/lohoff_2e_statistical_method_summary.md`\n- Figure reproduction note: `project/outputs/reports/lohoff_2e_repro_note.md`\n- Analysis scripts: `project/outputs/scripts/compute_lohoff_2e_stats.py`, `project/outputs/scripts/render_lohoff_2e_violin.py`, `project/outputs/scripts/finalize_lohoff_2e_violin.py`\n\n## References\n- Lohoff et al., seqFISH spatial transcriptomics mouse organogenesis study. DOI: [10.1038/s41587-021-01006-2](https://doi.org/10.1038/s41587-021-01006-2)\n", 'mode': 'overwrite'}, 'id': 'call_qeODyWD3V87z0MnRNEXLu9J4', 'type': 'tool_call'}

